+
+## Pose streaming and motion watchdog (local changes)
+
+The gamepad image now provides `/capabilities`, `/pose`, and `/heartbeat` with controller-specific 1500 ms motion leases. Boot is disarmed. An independent FreeRTOS task disables PWM when a lease expires; only explicit Start re-arms. Button routines run in a cancellable worker so HTTP handling remains responsive. The controller page sends its own heartbeat token; unrelated controller heartbeats cannot renew the active lease. Stop disables outputs regardless of lease owner.
+
+Build with `pio run -e gamepad -e calibration` from `code/`; flash the **gamepad** target for these features. No physical hardware tests or flashing were performed during development. PWM disable removes holding torque and may let the robot sag; use mechanical support during acceptance tests. Confirm servo calibration and limits before streaming arbitrary poses.
+
+Native lease regression test, from repository root:
+
+```bash
+g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Icode/include code/test/native/watchdog.cpp -o /tmp/kame-watchdog-test
+/tmp/kame-watchdog-test
+```
+
+The companion DanceMode/TeachMoves app includes complete setup and physical acceptance instructions in `FIRMWARE.md`.
